The code is good now because the DynamoDB lookup no longer uses the AWS_PROFILE set by each team's plan_infrastructure() pipeline.

Previously, when SIE ran with AWS_PROFILE=dev, the DynamoDB request was sent to the SIE dev AWS account, where dev-ImacConfigTable does not exist, causing the ResourceNotFoundException.

With the update:

AWS_PROFILE= AWS_DEFAULT_PROFILE= aws dynamodb get-item ...

the DynamoDB command ignores the team's profile and uses the Jenkins agent instance role, which has access to the correct account containing the DynamoDB table. At the same time, the original AWS_PROFILE remains available to identify the correct Terraform plan, such as dev.tfplan.
